# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The strip at the top of the screen is a MENU, not a picture of one: the
# system menu's rows do what the Deskbar's do, because both take the same
# command path.  The Deskbar answered these while the strip swallowed
# them, which is what a menu nobody wired looks like.
wait 18
note About opens the same window the leaf opens
click 20 8
wait 5
expect-menu About this system
menu-pick About this system
wait 12
expect-title About
key w ctrl
wait 6
note and Find opens the panel, from the strip as from anywhere else
click 20 8
wait 5
menu-pick Find
wait 12
expect-title Find
key Escape
wait 6
note Preferences opens Tracker's own, as Ctrl+comma does
click 20 8
wait 5
menu-pick Preferences
wait 12
expect-title TikuTracker preferences
key w ctrl
wait 6
